Not a bird identifier
---------------------

There is no trained acoustic model in this project and no audio capture at all. The eight "reference
calls" are SYNTHETIC six-band spectral sketches written by hand — not recordings, not derived from any
recording, and not measurements of any real bird.

What the app does: it ranks a sketch against those templates by Euclidean distance, converts the distance
to a confidence against the spread of the templates, and refuses to name a species below a threshold of
0.62 — saying "not a bird" instead. That ranking, the threshold, the refusal and the lifelist are real
and tested. The identification is not a real bird identification, and the app says so on its own face.

The species names are real species; the sketches are not their calls.
